From 3302a5b409ba40c218f2438d080fa2b3d2b5722c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 04:36:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: mt9t112: Add device tree and media controller
 support

Convert the driver from platform data and s_power to a modern subdevice:

- Add an of_match_table and parse the parallel endpoint with fwnode.
- Take the clock, regulators and optional reset GPIO from the device and
  use runtime PM with autosuspend instead of s_power.
- Select the PLL setup from the external clock rate (24 or 32 MHz) and
  program the reference count from it. Platform data users keep the
  divider they supplied.
- Register a media entity with one source pad, a subdev state with an
  init_state, and report pixel rate and link frequency controls.
- Add flip and test pattern controls.
- Retry the chip ID read after power up.

For the platform data path (ecovec24 with renesas-ceu, not tested),
set_fmt accepts the NULL active state and the bare try state without a
subdev that renesas-ceu passes. The driver now depends on
MEDIA_CONTROLLER and VIDEO_V4L2_SUBDEV_API, which VIDEO_RENESAS_CEU
does not select, so a CEU configuration without them loses the sensor.
Frame rate control is still missing.

